                <pb facs="0699" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg589"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5999: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >De Lambert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-09-25T16:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 25,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>64. Department’s telegram September 14, 4 p.m. Indications are that … has not
                    returned to Nicaragua. Foreign Office today informed me that he last Saturday
                    arrived at Las Juntas in southern Guanacaste with small theatrical troop and is
                    under surveillance.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Managua.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">De Lambert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
